fault-generic-failure = The operation failed. Check diagnostics and try again.
fault-revision-conflict = Settings changed. Refresh and try again.
fault-permission-denied = Permission denied. Check device authorization or contact the room administrator.
fault-unauthenticated = Pairing credentials are unavailable. Pair again.
fault-invalid-argument = The input is invalid. Check your settings and try again.
fault-not-found = The target no longer exists. Refresh the list.
fault-quota-exceeded = The allowed limit has been reached. Free resources and try again.
fault-receiver-busy = The AirPlay receiver is busy. Wait for the session to end or choose another receiver.
fault-room-capacity-full = The room is full. End another session and try again.
fault-source-already-active = This source already has an active session. Refresh to view it.
fault-source-blocked = This source is blocked. Contact the room administrator.
fault-pairing-revoked = Pairing was revoked. Pair again.
fault-stale-revision = Settings are out of date. Refresh and try again.
fault-session-changed = The source session changed. This action was not applied. Refresh and try again.
fault-output-unavailable = The selected output is unavailable. Check the device connection and output binding.
fault-worker-unavailable = The AirPlay worker is unavailable. Check the runtime installation and try again.
fault-upgrade-required = This version does not support the action. Update NeonMix.
fault-hub-port-in-use = Hub port { $port } is in use. Close the application using this port and try again.
fault-migration-required = Old pairing data needs offline migration. Run neonmix-credential-migrate.
fault-credential-missing = A credential file is missing. Restore the complete data directory or pair again.
fault-credential-permission-denied = Credential access was denied. Check the data directory permissions.
fault-credential-store-busy = Credentials are in use. Try again shortly.
fault-administrator-credential-protected = The Hub administrator credential is protected and cannot be removed through pairing.
fault-credential-io-failed = Credential files could not be read or written. Check the directory and disk.
fault-credential-corrupt = Pairing data is damaged. Restore a complete backup or pair again.
fault-credential-version-unsupported = The pairing data version is unsupported. Check the NeonMix version and migration instructions.
fault-credential-kind-mismatch = The credential type does not match this action. Select the correct pairing data.
fault-credential-reference-invalid = The credential reference is invalid. Restore the complete data directory.
fault-credential-already-exists = Credentials already exist. Use the existing data or choose a new directory.
fault-credential-profile-missing = The pairing profile is missing. Restore the complete data directory or pair again.
fault-setup-incomplete = Hub data is incomplete. Restore the complete directory and preserve the existing identity.
fault-unsupported-audio-format = The selected audio format is unsupported. Check the sample rate, channels, and buffer settings.
fault-capture-unavailable = Audio capture is unavailable. Check the virtual output and system permissions.
fault-connection-unavailable = The connection is unavailable. Check the Hub address and network diagnostics.
fault-background-timeout = The background request timed out. Check its status and try again.
fault-background-busy = The background is busy. Try again shortly.
fault-request-interrupted = The query was interrupted by a stop action. Run the query again if needed.
fault-background-shutting-down = The background is shutting down. Wait for it to finish.
fault-runtime-unavailable = A runtime program is unavailable. Check the installation files or finish the build.
fault-process-already-running = The audio process is still running or stopping. Wait for it to stop.
fault-process-exited = The audio process exited. Check diagnostics and restart it manually.
fault-stop-failed = The audio process could not be confirmed stopped. Check diagnostics and retry stopping.
fault-stop-incomplete = The audio process has not fully stopped. Retry stopping shortly.
fault-runtime-cleanup-incomplete = Audio stopped, but runtime key cleanup is incomplete. Check directory permissions and retry stopping.
fault-lifecycle-owner-lost = The audio lifecycle task is unavailable. Check the background status and diagnostics.
fault-hub-setup-exists = Hub data already exists. Edit the existing settings and preserve the established identity.
fault-hub-settings-require-stop = Stop Hub playback before editing its settings.
fault-sender-requires-hub-stop = This instance is playing audio. Stop the Hub before sending.
fault-hub-requires-sender-stop = This instance is sending audio. Stop sending before configuring or starting the Hub.
fault-self-connection-forbidden = This instance cannot connect to its own Hub. Use a separate Sender host.
fault-output-binding-required = No output binding exists. Add an output binding first.
fault-invalid-output-binding = The output binding is invalid. Check it or add it again.
fault-discovery-incomplete = Discovery did not return a complete result. Check the network and run discovery again.
fault-invalid-backend-response = The background returned an invalid result. Check the version and diagnostics, then try again.
fault-ipc-invalid-request = The background request is invalid. Check the desktop and background versions.
fault-ipc-incompatible-version = The desktop and background protocol versions are incompatible. Use one complete installation package.
fault-ipc-message-too-large = The result exceeds the communication limit. Reduce the scope or check diagnostics.
fault-invalid-path = The data path is invalid. Use a relative path inside the background data directory.
fault-diagnostics-save-failed = Diagnostics could not be saved. Check data directory permissions and free disk space.
fault-network-api-failed = Network configuration failed. Check installation files and network diagnostics, then run network repair again.
fault-network-identity-unavailable = Network configuration failed. Check installation files and network diagnostics, then run network repair again.
